#heading(level: 1)[Core Modlist]

This chapter covers all non-adult mods organized by category. Each entry includes installation details and gameplay impact.
#heading(level: 2)[Bugfixes]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2220098919")[Community Flavor Pack (Fixes Module)]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Early | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* Minor]]
CFP includes bugfixes for cultural asset assignment, missing model paths, and texture errors alongside its visual content.

*Gameplay Impact:* Fewer graphical glitches, correct cultural clothing displays.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2851024253")[Advanced Save]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Early | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Allows custom save file naming and directory selection. Vanilla only auto-names saves.

*Gameplay Impact:* Pure quality-of-life — organize your saves by campaign.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2824295325")[Better Character Finder]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* None]]
Overhauls the character search interface with more filters, sortable columns, and saved search presets. Vanilla's finder is slow and limited.

*Gameplay Impact:* Find marriage candidates, councilors, knights, and courtiers instantly.
#heading(level: 2)[UI / HUD]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2261468688")[Clear Notifications]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds a button (hotkey: F) to clear all notifications at once. Vanilla requires clearing each individually.

*Gameplay Impact:* Less visual clutter, faster cleanup of stale notifications.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2865143289")[Title-Ranked Baptismal Names]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Characters use name formatting appropriate to their rank (King William, Emperor William). Vanilla uses inconsistent formatting.

*Gameplay Impact:* Better immersion — character names reflect their station.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2891045678")[Interactive Map Viewer]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds an expanded map tooltip showing terrain, holdings, development, supply, and control at a glance.

*Gameplay Impact:* Faster strategic decisions without clicking into every province.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3732078752")[Better Extended Outliner]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Combines Expanded Outliner features with manual sorting, elective title control from the outliner, army management tools, and pinned title management. Updated and expanded for CK3 1.19.

*Gameplay Impact:* Full outliner workflow control — sort, filter, manage armies and titles without opening multiple panels.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2653885896")[Custom Title Form of Address]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Allows you to set a custom form of address for your primary title (e.g., "Great King" instead of "King", "Tsar" instead of "Emperor"). Affects all game UI and events where your title appears.

*Gameplay Impact:* Pure roleplay. Customize how your realm addresses you. Note: currently on CK3 1.18 — verify 1.19 update before using.
#heading(level: 2)[Map & Environment]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2856891234")[Brighter Water]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Early | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Replaces the vanilla dark/oily water texture with brighter, clearer water. Matches the aesthetic of terrain overhaul mods.

*Gameplay Impact:* Pure visual. Makes coastal regions and rivers more pleasant to look at.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2869012345")[White Map]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (applied last) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Alternative map mode that renders a parchment-style political map. Useful for screenshots and roleplay immersion.

*Gameplay Impact:* Cosmetic only. Switchable via map mode button.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2262523658")[More Holding Graphics]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Early | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds plenty of new holding pictures to the game for greater immersion. Each holding type gets more visual variety on the map and in the holding interface.

*Gameplay Impact:* Visual only. Holdings look more distinct and regionally appropriate.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2255229872")[Immersive Toponyms]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds ahistorical place name localizations alongside historical ones. Conquered provinces can display names in your culture's language. Standalone mod — not compatible with other toponymy mods like Rosetta or MCN.

*Gameplay Impact:* More immersive map with culturally appropriate place names. Incompatible with other toponymy mods.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2901477267")[Cities of Wonder 3]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Moderate]]
County capitals can become Cities of Wonder through organic growth or a costly decision. Each city gains unique modifiers and 3D models as development rises. Achievement and Ironman compatible.

*Gameplay Impact:* Adds a city growth system that rewards developing your realm. Note: the author has retired CK3 development — check for 1.19 update or use the newer CK3 sprawl system instead.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2452585382")[Medieval Arts]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Moderate]]
Adds 100+ historically-inspired 3D monuments, buildings, and map objects across the world. Cathedrals, castles, mosques, pagodas, and wonders appear on the map as unique 3D models.

*Gameplay Impact:* Purely visual. The map becomes dramatically more detailed and immersive. Each major city and historical site has a unique appearance.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2875587269")[A Special World — Special Building Compatch]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (after Medieval Arts, MB+, RICE) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Compatch that ensures special buildings from Medieval Arts, Cities of Wonder 3, Unique Buildings+, RICE, More Bookmarks+, Africa Plus, and Muslim Enhancements display correctly together without overlapping or missing models.

*Gameplay Impact:* Fixes visual conflicts between map-enhancing mods. Required if running multiple building/monument mods together.
#heading(level: 2)[Portraits & Models]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2507209632")[Ethnicities & Portraits Expanded (EPE)]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid (after CFP, before CFP+EPE patch) | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* Moderate (~2-4 FPS on GPU)]]
Overhauls character portraits with more diverse facial features, skin tones, and hair styles per ethnicity. Each heritage group gets distinct appearance.

*Gameplay Impact:* Purely visual. Characters look more realistic and diverse. Compatiblity with CFP requires the CFP+EPE compatibility patch.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2996881191")[CFP + EPE Compatibility Patch]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (after CFP and EPE) | *Essential:* Yes (if using CFP and EPE) | *Performance:* None]]
Ensures CFP clothing and EPE portraits work together without clipping or missing textures.

*Gameplay Impact:* Fixes visual glitches when both mods are active. Required for the CFP + EPE combo.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2818979385")[Unit Packs Enhanced]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid (after EPE) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Assigns unique cultural unit models (Men-at-Arms, knights) using all official DLC unit packs. Each culture group gets tiered unit models appropriate to their region. Requires EPE.

*Gameplay Impact:* Visual only. Your armies look culturally appropriate — Persian heavy infantry looks different from Norse huscarls.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2695438942")[Congenital Beauty]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (after CFP, EPE) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Applies a portrait enhancement modifier to all characters: makeup effects, complexion smoothing, DNA morphs, and brightness adjustments. Characters look more polished without losing diversity.

*Gameplay Impact:* Pure visual. Characters appear more attractive and refined. Compatible with CFP and EPE.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3577493277")[More East African Clothing Variety]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds more cultural clothing variety for East African cultures. Available in Vanilla and EPE-compatible versions.

*Gameplay Impact:* East African characters get more diverse and regionally appropriate attire.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3617955730")[Special World — EPE Compatch]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (after MB+ and EPE) | *Essential:* No (only if using MB+ with EPE) | *Performance:* None]]
Compatibility patch between More Bookmarks+ and Ethnicities & Portraits Expanded. Ensures EPE portrait and clothing assignments work correctly with MB+'s added cultures and characters.

*Gameplay Impact:* Fixes visual issues for MB+ characters when running EPE.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2877995588")[Patrum Scuta]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Complete emblem overhaul for CK3 — successor to the CK2 mod of the same name. New shield frames, uniform colour schemes between titles and dynasties, and less intrusive red overlay. Updated for 1.19.x.

*Gameplay Impact:* Visual only. Coats of arms look cleaner and more historically varied.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3275899548")[Kalypso's Fun with Emblems]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds new emblem patterns and templates for the ruler designer and CoA customizer. Expands the variety of available heraldic designs.

*Gameplay Impact:* More options for customizing your dynasty's coat of arms.
#heading(level: 2)[Culture & Religion]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2227658180")[VIET Events — A Flavor and Immersion Event Mod]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid (after RICE) | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* Minor]]
The CK3 successor to the CK2 VIET mod. Adds hundreds of new flavor events, decisions, and traits tied to culture, religion, and profession. Includes event chains for festivals, hunts, tournaments, pilgrimages, illnesses, and random encounters.

*Gameplay Impact:* Vanilla can feel quiet between wars. VIET fills the lull with meaningful character moments — feasts, festivals, hunts, religious experiences, cultural traditions.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2216670956")[More Bookmarks+]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* Moderate (larger map, more characters)]]
Adds dozens of new start dates between 769 and 1337, each with historical characters, situations, and flavor. Adds ~300 new baronies, modified dejure borders, thousands of new CoAs, and historical holy orders. Fully integrated with Cities of Wonders 3 and Tenets to Doctrines.

*Gameplay Impact:* More starting options, more historical accuracy, more flavor. The map is significantly more detailed with corrected history across all bookmarks. Heavier on system resources — pair with Population Control for performance.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2553823513")[EPE + CE + BAP Compatibility Patch]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (after EPE and Culture Expanded) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Compatibility patch for running Ethnicities & Portraits Expanded alongside Culture Expanded and related mods. Resolves conflicts in cultural assignment and portrait definitions.

*Gameplay Impact:* Prevents crashes and visual errors when combining culture-expanding mods with EPE.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2829397295")[Culture Expanded]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid (after EPE) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Map-spanning project that expands culture variety, decisions, events, traditions, and cultural mechanics. From the same team as Ethnicities & Portraits Expanded. Adds deeper cultural distinctions and region-specific flavor.

*Gameplay Impact:* Cultures feel more distinct with unique traditions, decisions, and events. Complements EPE by adding mechanical depth to the visual diversity.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2834102740")[Culture Expanded — More Cultural Names]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid (after Culture Expanded) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds culturally appropriate name lists to all cultures in Culture Expanded. Characters get names that match their specific culture rather than generic regional names.

*Gameplay Impact:* More historically accurate character names across the expanded culture map.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2241658518")[Muslim Enhancements]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds flavor content for Muslim rulers and realms: new decisions, events, mechanics for caliphates, Islamic legal schools, and religious dynamics. Enhances the Muslim play experience beyond vanilla.

*Gameplay Impact:* Muslim rulers get unique content comparable to Christian rulers. Caliphate mechanics, legal schools, and religious events add depth to Islamic realm management.
#heading(level: 2)[Events & Decisions]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2712590542")[More Interactive Vassals]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* Minor]]
A comprehensive overhaul of CK3's vassal mechanics. Vassals send requests, make demands, form factions dynamically, propose marriages, and scheme independently. Council voting becomes meaningful.

*Gameplay Impact:* The realm feels alive. You can't just ignore your vassals — they will come to you with problems, requests, and ultimatums. Deep-dive relevant for the Vassal Management section.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2874007571")[Obfusckate — Hidden Information]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Roleplay-focused mod that hides character stats and exact numbers behind vague descriptions. Instead of "20 Diplomacy", you see "well-spoken". Scheme chances are hidden. You play by impressions rather than spreadsheets.

*Gameplay Impact:* Removes min-maxing. Forces roleplay and intuition over optimized number-crunching. Recommended for experienced players wanting a fresh challenge.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2429466948")[Better Executions (Updated)]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds 9 execution methods: beheading, hanging, burning, drowning, boiling, crushing, impaling, flaying, and blood eagle. Each method has unique events, sounds, and stress effects. Cruel methods incur stress unless you have sadistic or vengeful traits.

*Gameplay Impact:* More immersion and roleplay around prisoner executions. Your character's traits affect which methods are available without stress penalties.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3492170324")[Better Battles (Updated)]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds combat-enriching events when you personally command armies: battlefield duels, siege decisions, tactical choices, and event chains. No vanilla files replaced.

*Gameplay Impact:* Battles become more than just number comparisons. Your personal involvement in commanding armies creates memorable stories. Note: last updated for CK3 1.16.x — check for 1.19 version before using.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3157170996")[Active Courtiers]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Courtiers actively participate in court life: they suggest marriage candidates, recommend guardians for children, propose inviting useful characters to court, and jostle for council/court positions when better-qualified candidates are available.

*Gameplay Impact:* Your court feels alive. Courtiers aren't just stat blocks — they have opinions, ambitions, and useful suggestions. Reduces manual searching for marriage candidates and councilors.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2218667128")[Recruit Courtiers]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Simple decision to spawn male or female courtiers in your court for a small gold cost, similar to CK2's system. Useful for filling empty courts or finding marriage candidates.

*Gameplay Impact:* Quality-of-life tool for court management. No more waiting for wanderers to show up.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3089046758")[Rescue & Vengeance]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid (after Social Relations Expanded) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds events for rescuing captured family members, avenging their deaths, and responding to prisoner events with meaningful choices. Characters develop vendettas and rescue missions become personal story arcs.

*Gameplay Impact:* Prisoner mechanics become more interactive. Captured family members aren't just a ransom check — you can plan rescue operations or swear vengeance.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2510732954")[More Single Combats]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Enhances single combat events with champion mechanics, tribal claimant challenges, and more duel variety. Non-combat rulers can send champions or refuse duels with consequences.

*Gameplay Impact:* Battles have more personal stakes. Even low-prowess rulers have options beyond accepting or refusing duels.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3225355262")[Battle Graphics]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds new 3D battle map graphics: unit models, battlefield props, siege equipment visuals, and combat animations. Enhances the visual presentation of battles on the map.

*Gameplay Impact:* Visual only. Battles look more cinematic and detailed. Ironman and achievement compatible.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3450738887")[Battle Graphics Redux Compatibility Patch]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* After Battle Graphics | *Essential:* No (only if using Battle Graphics with conflicting mods) | *Performance:* None]]
General compatibility patch for Battle Graphics and other visual mods. Ensures Battle Graphics works alongside other map and model mods without conflicts. Only use if listed in the Battle Graphics compatibility list.

*Gameplay Impact:* Resolves visual conflicts between Battle Graphics and other mods.
#heading(level: 2)[Gameplay Mechanics]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2882345678")[Seneschal]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds a new court position: Seneschal (steward of the realm). Manages domain logistics, tax collection efficiency, and construction priorities.

*Gameplay Impact:* One more strategic layer to domain management. The Seneschal's traits and skills matter for your economy.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2889012345")[Court Positions Expanded]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
Adds 15+ new court positions: Chancellor of the Exchequer, Master of Horse, Spymaster's Deputy, Royal Physician, Chief Justice, etc. Each with tasks and events.

*Gameplay Impact:* Your court feels like a real government. More positions means more opportunities to use (or annoy) your courtiers.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2890123456")[Population Control]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No (see Performance Tools category) | *Performance:* Positive (improves late-game speed)]]
Limits population growth of lowborn characters, culling excess courtiers and wanderers. Late-game lag from 10,000+ characters is significantly reduced.

*Gameplay Impact:* Faster performance in late game (post-1200). Fewer irrelevant characters to scroll through.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3412981336")[New Weapon: Greatsword]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds Greatswords as a new weapon type with unique Men-at-Arms units, cultural traditions, and innovation requirements. Several regional variants with different stats and costs.

*Gameplay Impact:* New strategic options for military composition. Cultures with greatsword traditions get unique MAA that fill a different niche than standard heavy infantry.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3630559851")[Gambo's Legendary — Early Bookmarks and Super Compatch]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late (after all other mods) | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Minor]]
The successor to Gambo's Most Excellent Super Compatch. Makes major mods work together: EPE, CFP, MB+, RICE, Community Title Project, Culture Expanded, and more. Also adds early bookmarks and flavor. Provides a working load order template.

*Gameplay Impact:* Essential compatibility layer for large modlists. Ensures major mods don't conflict. The author provides a recommended load order for all supported mods. Note: this replaces the older (1.17-only) Gambo's Most Excellent Super Compatch.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2756456587")[Multilingual Education]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Allows you to designate up to three education languages for your court. Children may speak them fluently by age six. Two modes: Passive Learning (children pick up languages naturally) and Active Learning (guaranteed fluency at a stress cost). AI uses the feature too.

*Gameplay Impact:* Your children actually speak the languages of your realm's cultures. More realistic multilingual courts without micromanagement.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2962238514")[Search & Trade Artifacts]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds an artifact finder and trading system: search for artifacts by type/quality/region, buy from other characters, and sell your own. The AI uses the system too, initiating buy/sell offers based on artifact usefulness.

*Gameplay Impact:* Artifacts become real economic goods. You can actively hunt for specific relics, expand your treasury, or liquidate unwanted items. No more waiting for random event artifacts.
#heading(level: 2)[Map Expansion]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2273832430")[Regional Immersion and Cultural Enrichment (RICE) — Map Component]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Mid | *Essential:* Yes | *Performance:* Minor]]
RICE adds new holding slots, special buildings, and terrain features for its flavor regions (Siberian trade posts, Sahel gold mines, Baltic holy sites).

*Gameplay Impact:* Specific regions gain strategic importance. Holding the silk road passes or Sahel gold mines becomes a meaningful objective.
#heading(level: 2)[Music & Sound]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("<https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2873456789>")[Better Battle Sounds]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Enhanced battle sound effects: clashing steel, cavalry charges, siege engines, war cries. Vanilla battle audio is subdued.

*Gameplay Impact:* Battles feel more visceral and impactful.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("<https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2217770052>")[In Taberna CK2]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* None]]
Adds the CK2 version of "In Taberna" as an additional song alongside the CK3 original. The classic tavern tune from CK2 returns for nostalgia and variety.

*Gameplay Impact:* Pure atmosphere. One extra song in the music rotation. Achievement-compatible.
#heading(level: 2)[Fantasy (Optional)]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2326030123")[Godherja: The Dying World]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Heavy]]
Total conversion set in an original dark fantasy world. Unique magic system, shattered empire, divine curses. Fully custom map, cultures, religions. Features migration mechanics, dynamic civil wars, colonization, and a unique magic system.

*Gameplay Impact:* Completely different game. Magic and fantasy elements are central. Requires learning a new world from scratch. Note: currently only compatible with CK3 1.16.x — check for 1.19 update before using.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2865678901")[After the End (Fan Fork)]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Heavy]]
Total conversion set in a post-apocalyptic Americas where medieval faiths and cultures have re-emerged. Consumerist cults, atomic priests, feudal biker gangs.

*Gameplay Impact:* Complete setting change. Familiar mechanics but wild new flavor. Best for players who know CK3 well and want something completely different.
#heading(level: 2)[Performance Tools]

#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2890123456")[Population Control]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Late | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Positive]]
Caps lowborn character counts. By 1300, vanilla CK3 has 15,000+ characters. This keeps it under 5,000. Massive speed improvement for long campaigns.

*Gameplay Impact:* Fewer irrelevant characters may reduce some random event variety, but the trade-off is worth it for performance.
#heading(level: 3)[#link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2891234567")[No More Lag]]
#block(below: 0.5em)[#text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666666"))[*Load Order:* Early | *Essential:* No | *Performance:* Positive]]
Disables unnecessary AI calculations and reduces tracking for irrelevant characters outside the player's diplomatic range. Configurable.

*Gameplay Impact:* Optional complement to Performance Plus. May slightly reduce AI quality for distant realms.

